 "verdict": "CROSSES 300 ct BUT STAYS BELOW 2000 ct. 4.91 % of engaged frames (12.2 s) sit ABOVE the first knot, reaching 1389 ct (E1) / 1496 ct (E4 upper bound). \u21d2 THE HEADLINE CLAIM 'the operating point sits ENTIRELY INSIDE THE FLAT FIRST SEGMENT' IS FALSE. The 2000 knot is NOT reached, so a Y[0]+Y[1] edit creates NO SLOPE DISCONTINUITY anywhere the car goes and the candidate is NOT B1-class. BUT THE EDIT IS NOT A CLEAN SCALAR EITHER: with Y[2] left unscaled, the delivered dose is FULL below 300 ct (95.1 % of engaged frames) and FADES LINEARLY toward 1.000x as the index approaches 2000. On the quoted Y1=256/Y2=225, a nominal 2.000x delivers 1.84x at 600 ct, 1.50x at 1200 ct and 1.32x at the measured peak -- only about a third of the intended increment survives at peak rate. THE FIX IS ONE MORE CELL: scale Y[2] too, which moves the seam into the 2000-4000 segment that the car never visits and restores a clean scalar over the whole reachable range for 2 more bytes."
